     in via data-hero-entrance — GH #172, its poster can't be the LCP
     element) — but the rules themselves live in styles/motion.css. The
     html.js gate can't survive
     Astro's scoped-style compiler (a bare :where(html.js) gets the scope
     attribute fused onto html, and :where(:global(html.js)) emits an empty
     :where(); both silently deaden the selector), and unscoped the
     specificity also stays below the revealed fade-out below so it keeps
